00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:50,550
Guess not.

256
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:57,200
The other day, I rode a real-life
shark. A shark? Are you kidding?

257
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,457
Chomsky, Inosaki, rode him too.

258
00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:01,128
It is as rough as they say.

259
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:03,900
That's crazy.

260
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:12,917
They couldn't keep a conversation
going if their lives depended on it.

261
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,757
I already knew that, but still!

262
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:18,137
Not to mention they're from two
different worlds with nothing in common.

263
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:19,877
We're playing on hard mode.

264
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:22,937
They didn't have much
trouble talking on the trip,

265
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:25,900
but now that it's just
them, they're clamming

266
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:28,597
up at this rate.

267
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:29,897
A rift will form between them.

268
00:18:29,980 --> 00:18:31,737
This is bad!

269
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:35,717
I tried butting out, but
they leave me no choice.

270
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:38,737
Time to take charge and
revive this conversation.

271
00:18:38,820 --> 00:18:40,957
Listen, you two!

272
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:42,940
Allow me

273
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:46,617
to demonstrate a new party
trick I came up with.

274
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:49,977
You do remember last time, right?

275
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:51,120
That was rough!

276
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:56,057
I'm sorry, but if the mood gets any more
hellish, even I won't be able to help.

277
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:56,970
Right ahead.

278
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,000
I'd like to see it.

279
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:04,218
God, what are you going to do, Gero?

280
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:07,860
Spew liquid DIY candy out of your mouth?

281
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:11,085
Please don't ruin your
chances with an Eshinou.

282
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:30,820
Hey, this flower matches my scarf.

283
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:32,440
Oh, I love these!

284
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:37,007
I used to think all a party trick
had to do was get attention.

285
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:39,675
Just goes to show you how much I know.

286
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:42,277
But you taught me.

287
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:43,980
I got to see that actually.

288
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:48,124
The whole point is to do something
that entertains you, you know?

289
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:51,997
Mr. Kato.

290
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:54,617
I came up with a new trick
too, if you want to see.

291
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:56,200
I think you'll like it!

292
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:08,357
They might suck at
talking but if they found

293
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:10,817
